				466,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add event emission argument DTO for language provider RPC\n\nIntroduces `EmitProviderEventArgument` struct to handle event propagation from extension hosts to Mountain core via Vine IPC. This DTO enables:\n- Tracking provider event sources through numeric `EventHandle`\n- Carrying provider-specific event payloads via generic `EventArgument` field\n- Structured deserialization of RPC arguments using serde attributes\n\nSupports MVP Path A extension capabilities by enabling communication patterns required for VS Code-compatible language features (e.g. code lenses, diagnostics). The handle-based approach aligns with recent extension state management work in commit cc4df7d while maintaining separation between Cocoon-side shims and Mountain's native handlers.",
			"SHA": "76d8e58acc1a46a9d6240ca3988a1309fdf5a27a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-06T23:47:52Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				464,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "f4a547dc10d178927c3de1dcdc9f4c53cb020258"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-06T23:47:50Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				463,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add RPC argument DTOs for extension enablement state management\n\n- Introduce `GetEnablementStateArgument` and `SetEnablementArgument` structs as Data Transfer Objects\n- Formalizes RPC message formats for extension enablement/disablement operations between `Sky` UI and `Mountain` backend\n- Enables implementation of extension state persistence through `Track` dispatcher and `AppState` management\n- Follows Rust naming conventions with PascalCase structs to match `Echo` API contract requirements\n- Supports MVP Path A (`Cocoon` sidecar) by establishing foundation for extension lifecycle management RPCs\n- Positions for future `Grove` integration by creating clear separation between RPC contracts and implementation",
			"SHA": "cc4df7d821fbcf09f62b54af1e2301c0f4ddc961"
		},
