			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				408,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add diagnostics management RPC argument DTOs\n\nIntroduces structured argument DTOs for diagnostics RPC operations in Mountain's IPC layer, specifically supporting:\n- GetDiagnosticsArgument for querying active diagnostics\n- ChangeManyArgument for batch diagnostic updates\n\nThis implements critical serialization structures for the Vine IPC transport layer, enabling Cocoon sidecar extensions to report and manage code problems through Mountain's native handlers. The DTO patterns follow established conventions from recent RPC argument implementations (fd59672, f785591) while focusing on diagnostic-specific requirements.\n\nContributes to MVP Path A deliverables by expanding the IPC surface needed for VS Code extension compatibility through Cocoon shims. The strongly typed arguments ensure reliable JSON serialization/deserialization across the stdio boundary between Mountain and Node.js sidecars.",
			"SHA": "ea0098b17ce7a1ce4d9b53055be81358ca387f96"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-06T23:44:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				406,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add configuration management RPC argument DTOs\n\nIntroduces structured argument definitions for configuration-related RPC operations between Mountain and Cocoon sidecar. Contains DTO modules for:\n- GetConfigurationArgument with OverridesDto\n- InspectArgument\n- UpdateArgument\n\nThese types enable type-safe serialization/deserialization of configuration management requests through Vine IPC, supporting the implementation of VS Code-compatible configuration APIs in Cocoon shims. The argument structures follow platform-agnostic design principles established in previous Vine IPC work, ensuring compatibility with both current Node.js sidecar and potential future native runtimes.\n\nThis contributes to MVP Path A deliverables by building out the configuration management system required for extension host compatibility, while maintaining architectural alignment with Land's phased evolution strategy.",
			"SHA": "fd59672ea90189ca27cfd38c8c15bfbd31ea963b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
