				396,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add lifecycle management for Cocoon gRPC server\n\n- Introduces initialization and state management for Cocoon's gRPC server in Mountain's IPC layer\n- Implements idempotent startup pattern with proper error handling and cleanup procedures\n- Enables reliable communication channel setup between Mountain backend and Cocoon sidecar\n- Supports MVP Path A requirements by establishing critical IPC infrastructure for VS Code extension compatibility\n- Integrates with CancellationTokenRegistry for coordinated operation cancellation\n- Provides graceful shutdown handling to maintain process integrity during restarts\n- Follows recent Vine component enhancements (gRPC handlers, binary data support) to complete server lifecycle management",
			"SHA": "af61b47a92020af3875c432a86e283ab35f15ac6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-06T23:42:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				395,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Add handler for receiving binary RPC data from Mountain\n\nImplements server-side gRPC handler in Mountain's IPC layer to process raw binary payloads from the Cocoon sidecar. This enables:\n- Reliable delivery of VS Code extension protocol messages via Vine's gRPC transport\n- Integration with RPCProtocol._receiveMessage callback for extension host communication\n- Error handling and logging for data deserialization failures\n- Immediate acknowledgement to maintain bidirectional communication flow\n\nThis forms critical infrastructure for MVP Path A's extension support, allowing Cocoon to forward extension messages through Mountain's native IPC while maintaining compatibility with VS Code's existing RPC mechanisms. The buffer validation and callback architecture align with Land's focus on stable extension host communication in the Cocoon sidecar implementation.",
			"SHA": "4b4cd9ad0006ad4974b1c42f1190e28171e687d5"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2025-06-06T23:41:57Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				394,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Vine): Implement server handler for Cocoon gRPC requests\n\nAdd core request handling logic for Mountain's gRPC server supporting Cocoon communication. The new HandleRequest.ts:\n- Processes incoming unary RPC calls from Mountain backend\n- Converts Protobuf parameters to JS values using shared ProtoValueConverter\n- Dispatches requests to central message handler via DispatchMessage\n- Implements error handling with GRPC status codes for parameter conversion and processing failures\n- Integrates with generated Vine gRPC service definitions\n\nThis forms the server-side counterpart to recent Vine client implementations (2ff0d1d, 06588b7), completing the bidirectional IPC flow needed for Cocoon<->Mountain extension operations. The handler enables Cocoon shims to proxy extension API calls through Vine IPC, advancing MVP Path A's extension support capabilities (Deliverable #5). Detailed logging and type safety checks align with Land's reliability goals while maintaining compatibility with VS Code extension expectations.",
			"SHA": "4d6a528c47fac3f15ca93b10dae16aa8ab14c750"
		},
		{
